History and traditions of philosophy (@history-and-traditions-of-philosophy: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_17Q7Z11WNMH2ZWVXCZT2ASB2RK
The history of philosophy investigates how questions, arguments, texts, and traditions developed and were reinterpreted. This material connects ancient, medieval, modern, and contemporary philosophy through particular problems and primary works, including analytic, dialectical, phenomenological, hermeneutic, pragmatic, and critical approaches and Brazilian and Latin American debates. Use historical context, translations, commentary, and disagreements to understand an argument before comparing it across periods. Offer both chronological routes and routes following one question through several traditions.

**Parent:** [Philosophy](../Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001).
